      "question": "Why is raw pixel-wise comparison brittle for checking whether two face images show the same person?",
      "stem_format": "plain_text",
      "choices_format": "plain_text",
      "choices": [
        "Pixel values are constant across cameras, so they cannot represent differences between people.",
